  'mode.bd10.name':'Backdash 10s', 'mode.bd10.desc':()=>'Measures how far you retreat with backdashes in 10 seconds (m, the same unit as the in-game practice distance). Backdash with 4 N 4, cut the recovery with 1 (d/b) and roll straight from 1 into 4: 414 N 414 N … A backdash starts slow, retreats fastest around 6–11f and stops at '+BD_LAST+'f (a full backdash is '+BD_FULL.toFixed(2)+' m). The best cancel is '+BD.CANCEL_A+'–'+BD.CANCEL_B+'f; without a cancel the next backdash is locked for '+BD.RECOVER_F+'f. A 2 (d) or 8 (u) cancel is a sidestep and drops your guard. Distances are community measurements (Tekken 8, Mishima-style character average).',
  'hint.bd10':()=>'4 N 4 → 1 (d/b) → 4 N 4 … best cancel at '+BD.CANCEL_A+'–'+BD.CANCEL_B+'f · roll 1 straight into 4 · 2/8 = sidestep (drops guard)',
  'trial.bdProg':(n,d)=>n+' backdashes · '+d+' m', 'trial.bdEnd':(d,n)=>'10s over · '+d+' m ('+n+' backdashes)',
  'rec.dist':d=>d+' m', 'rec.bdSub':(n,t,c)=>n+' backdashes · '+t+' very fast · best chain '+c,
  'card.dist':'Distance', 'card.backdashes':'Backdashes', 'card.top':'Very fast',
  'log.tBack':'Backdash', 'res.bd_top':'Very fast', 'res.bd_fast':'Fast', 'res.bd_ok':'OK', 'res.bd_slow':'Slow',
  'bd.grade.top':'Very fast', 'bd.grade.fast':'Fast', 'bd.grade.ok':'OK', 'bd.grade.slow':'Slow',
  'bd.title':(n,g)=>'Backdash ×'+n+' · '+g, 'bd.first.title':'Backdash', 'bd.first.sub':f=>'4 N 4 in '+f+'f · now cut the recovery with 1 (d/b) and roll straight into 4',
  'bd.sub':(mps,h,hand,best)=>mps+' m/s · cancel '+h+'f · hand '+hand+'f (best cancel for it '+best+'f)',
  'bd.cancel':(h,off,d)=>'cancel '+h+'f ('+(off===0?'optimal':(off>0?'+':'')+off+'f')+') · '+d+' m', 'bd.log.cancel':h=>'cancel '+h+'f',
  'bd.chain.end':n=>'backdash chain '+n,
  'bd.coach.first':()=>'The backdash is out. Keep holding 4 and cut the recovery with <strong>1 (d/b)</strong> at <strong>'+BD.CANCEL_A+'–'+BD.CANCEL_B+'f</strong>, then roll straight from 1 into <strong>4</strong>, N, 4 for the next one.',
  'bd.coach.early':(n,best,hand)=>'The cancel is <strong>'+n+'f</strong> early. With a '+hand+'f hand, cutting at '+best+'f is fastest — the backdash covers most ground around 6–11f, so do not throw that away.',
  'bd.coach.late':(n,best,hand)=>'The cancel is <strong>'+n+'f</strong> late. With a '+hand+'f hand, cutting at '+best+'f is fastest — after that it barely moves, so put the 1 (d/b) in right away.',
  'bd.coach.db':n=>'1 (d/b) was held <strong>'+n+'f</strong> too long. Once the crouch registers, roll straight into 4.',
  'bd.coach.tap':n=>'The gap inside 4 N 4 is <strong>'+n+'f</strong> long. Tap 4, release, and 4 again at once.',
  'bd.coach.cancelOk':'Good cancel timing. Now roll straight from 1 into 4, N, 4.', 'bd.coach.good':'A clean set. Keep this rhythm.',
  'bd.coach.cancelEarly':n=>'The cancel is <strong>'+n+'f</strong> before the window. The backdash covers most ground around 6–11f, so hold 4 until '+BD.CANCEL_A+'f.', 'bd.coach.cancelLate':n=>'The cancel is <strong>'+n+'f</strong> after the window. Past '+BD.CANCEL_B+'f it barely moves.', 'bd.f.crouch.title':'Stopped on 1 (set over)',
  'bd.f.noCancel.title':'No cancel', 'bd.f.noCancel.sub':()=>'The backdash ran to the end. The next backdash is locked for '+BD.RECOVER_F+'f', 'bd.f.noCancel.coach':()=>'Cut the recovery with <strong>1 (d/b)</strong> before you release 4. Without it the next 4 N 4 will not come out during the '+BD.RECOVER_F+'f recovery.',
  'bd.f.stiff.title':'Still recovering (no backdash)', 'bd.f.stiff.coach':()=>'The previous backdash was not cancelled, so you are still in its '+BD.RECOVER_F+'f recovery. Only backing up is locked — a 1 (d/b) after each backdash lets the next one come out at once.',
  'bd.f.side.title':'Sidestep cancel (guard dropped)', 'bd.f.side.coach':'2 (d) and 8 (u) are sidesteps: they cancel too, but your guard drops. Sit down with 1 (d/b) instead.',
  'bd.f.neutral1.title':'Neutral after 1', 'bd.f.neutral1.coach':'Do not let go of 1 (d/b) — roll straight into <strong>4</strong>. Passing through neutral breaks the set: 41<u>4</u> N 414 N …',
  'bd.f.dir.title':'Other direction', 'bd.f.dir.coach':'Another direction slipped into 4 N 4. Tap 4, release, 4 again.',
  'bd.f.tapLong.title':'4 held too long', 'bd.f.tapLong.coach':'Tap the first 4 and release it at once. Holding it is a back walk.',
  'bd.f.nLong.title':'Neutral too long', 'bd.f.nLong.coach':'The second 4 came too late after the release to pair into a backdash. 4 N 4 faster.',
  'bdp.timeline':'Backdash frame timeline', 'bdp.evaluation':'Set review', 'bdp.recent':'Recent sets', 'bdp.help':'Formula and sources',
  'bdp.gradeCol':'Grade', 'bdp.cutCol':'Cancel', 'bdp.handCol':'Hand', 'bdp.speedCol':'m/s',
  'bdp.guide':(a,b,hand,last,rec,db,tap)=>'1f = the frame the backdash comes out (second 4, counted from 1 like startup frames). Cell fill = distance retreated so far. The best cancel timing is '+a+'–'+b+'f (earlier for a faster hand); after it, aim for a 1 (d/b) hold of '+db+'f + a 4 N 4 of '+tap+'f = '+hand+'f. The strips under the axis are this set\'s 1 hold and 4 N 4. The backdash stops at '+last+'f; without a cancel the next one can only come out from '+rec+'f.',
  'bdp.legend':'Gold cell = the frame of your 1 (d/b) · underlined number = the best cancel frame for this hand speed · red cells = the backdash coming out (1f) and the next one · fill = distance travelled · SLOWING = almost stopped, holding longer gains nothing',
  'bdp.bandMove':'MOVE', 'bdp.bandCancel':'BEST CANCEL', 'bdp.bandTail':'SLOWING', 'bdp.bandStill':'STOPPED', 'bdp.spanDb':(g,n)=>g+' '+n+'f', 'bdp.spanTap':n=>'4N4 '+n+'f',
  'bdp.liveReady':'Backdash with 4 N 4', 'bdp.liveDone':'Waiting for the next backdash',
