  'app.docTitle':'Mishima Dojo | Tekken EWGF & Wave Dash Trainer',
  'app.description':"Practice Tekken EWGF and wave dashes for free in your browser. Check your input timing and improve your personal best. Keyboard and gamepad support. No installation needed.",
  'og.chipWave':'wave', 'og.chipEwgf':'EWGF', 'og.altNames':'미시마 도장 · 三島道場',
  'og.line1':'Tekken EWGF & wave dash practice', 'og.line2':'Frame-accurate judging in your browser',
  'og.keywords':'EWGF trainer · wave dash practice · free · keyboard / gamepad',
  'og.footer':"Same 60Hz frame · timing histogram · trials · share cards",
  'footer':'Notation: 6 = forward (f), N = neutral, 2 = down (d), 3 = down-forward (d/f), button 2 = right punch (RP). Wave = 6N23 6 N 6N23 6 N … (the 6 after 3 cancels the recovery). 1 frame = 16.67ms. Unofficial fan-made practice tool.',
  'footer.copy':'© 2026 master_shin. All rights reserved. No copying, modification or redistribution of the source, artwork or audio.', 'footer.contact':'Contact',
  'about.summary':'What is Mishima Dojo? (About · how judging works · FAQ)',
  'about.what.h':'Free Tekken 8 EWGF and wave dash trainer',
  'about.what.p':'Mishima Dojo is a free browser tool for the two inputs every Mishima-style character in Tekken (Tekken 8) lives on: the Electric Wind God Fist (EWGF, f,N,d,d/f+2, written 6N23+2 here) and the wave dash (crouch dash chains, 6N23 6 N 6N23 6 N …). Nothing to install: it works with a keyboard, gamepad or hitbox/leverless, and it judges your inputs without the game running. It is an unofficial fan-made tool, not a macro or a cheat, and it never touches the game.',
  'about.judge.h':'How judging works',
  'about.judge.p':"EWGF rounds each input timestamp onto a shared 60Hz grid: d/f and RP in the same frame succeed; RP in a later frame is WGF and in an earlier frame is a miss. Wave dash accepts f, N, d, d/f or f, d, d/f, with separate cancel and starting forward inputs. Dedicated wave-cancel practice pairs back on frame 8/9/10 counting d/f as frame 1 with RP at 1/1–2/1–3f. The browser grid is not synchronized to game frames; input devices have different timing errors.",
  'about.modes.h':'Timed modes and the leaderboard',
  'about.modes.p':'Besides free practice there are Wave 10s, EWGF ×20, Wave EWGF ×10, Dummy Rush 30s and Backdash 10s. Results are charted as a button-timing histogram and a wave speed trend. Pick a nickname to post to the leaderboard, compare with other players and get a tier (SS to D) from your top percentage. Result cards can be saved as images for sharing.',
  'about.faq.h':'FAQ',
  'about.q1':'My EWGF keeps coming out as a normal WGF.',
  'about.a1':'Your 2 is landing after d/f. Watch the ms offset in the result and press 2 as you roll from d into d/f, not after d/f is fully in.',
  'about.q2':'My wave dash keeps breaking.',
  'about.a2':'Usually the cancel f after d/f is missing, or that f is reused as the next dash\'s starting f so the neutral never registers. The result panel names the fault ("Missing cancel 6", "Missing start 6").',
  'about.q3':'Does it work with a stick or on a phone?',
  'about.a3':'Any controller the browser recognises as a gamepad can have its directions and buttons remapped in settings. Keyboard and leverless are confirmed; sticks vary by device, so get in touch if yours reads wrong. Phones get touch controls, with lower precision.',
  'about.q4':'Where is my data stored?',
  'about.a4':'Settings and practice records are stored in this browser. Using server features sends your nickname, authentication details, leaderboard records, posts and votes. Details are in the privacy policy below.',
  'about.q5':'Is it free?',
  'about.a5':'Completely free. It runs on donations, and ads may be shown to cover running costs.',
  'about.links':'Practice in your language',
