  'gp.guide':(hit,rec,free,target,buf)=>'Press RP with d/f held; for the '+rec+' frames of recovery that follow, nothing at all comes out. The only direction that survives it is the start f — press it inside the last '+buf+' frames — and the neutral has to be made by letting go on frame '+free+', where the recovery ends. Then d/f+RP, and the EWGF landing by frame '+target+' is the success. The '+hit+'f startup, '+rec+'f recovery and '+buf+'f buffer are unverified assumptions, and actual hit or punish timing is not measured.',

  'gp.spanStartup':n=>'startup '+n+'f',
  'gp.spanRec':n=>'recovery '+n+'f',
  "gp.bandBuf":"Pre-input", "gp.bandFree":"Neutral", "gp.bandFire":"Attack",
  'gp.challengeHint':n=>n+'-try challenge: the next '+n+' judged links give a success rate and a best streak. Interrupted tries do not count, and only a finished run is posted to the leaderboard (successes, then best streak).',
  'gp.legend':(hit,free,target,near)=>'Red '+hit+'f: counter hit · dimmed: the startup and recovery spans, one cell each · '+near+' grey cells: the start f pre-input window, any frame in it · gold '+free+'f: neutral, this one frame · coral '+target+'f: the attack, the EWGF fires here',
  'gp.note':(target,rec,buf,free)=>`There is one criterion: did the EWGF after the d/f+2 come out by frame ${target} (verified in game). The command route is not looked at, so 6N23, 623 and the mist-step 6N3 all qualify as long as the input is accepted as an EWGF. For the ${rec} frames of recovery after a d/f+2 nothing comes out at all — no walking, no dash, no move. The only direction that survives the recovery is the start f; everything from the neutral on has to go in after it ends, so letting go of the f inside the recovery throws that neutral away. Buttons are the same: only the last one pressed inside the final ${buf} frames survives and comes out on the frame the recovery ends (a one-slot buffer, last input wins, anything earlier is dropped). So the hands do this: hold f through the recovery, release it on frame ${free} where the recovery ends, then d/f+RP on frame ${target}. The neutral and start f positions are shown alongside as reference values for what ran late. The bag always stands alone, in range. d/f+2 itself has no just frame and is never timed. Judging and presentation are the same as in every other mode, and an EWGF landed here still counts toward the ordinary EWGF stats. Session records are lost on refresh. Only a finished 10-try challenge reaches the leaderboard.`,
