  'jf.guide':'Roll f → n → d/f and press 4 on the same 60Hz frame as the d/f. Going through d is a normal Sky Rocket. A JF in the middle of a wavedash is accepted for practice (the game does not allow it).',
  'jf.fLabel':'Forward', 'jf.nLabel':'Neutral', 'jf.rkLabel':'d/f ↔ 4', 'jf.resultLabel':'Result', 'jf.oneTarget':'target 1f', 'jf.rkTarget':'target same frame', 'jf.resultTarget':'success = same frame',
  'jf.fastestCount':'Fastest', 'jf.recent':'Recent tries', 'jf.fnCol':'f / n', 'jf.rkCol':'d/f ↔ 4', 'jf.help':'How the JF Sky Rocket is judged',
  'jf.note':'The same shared 60Hz grid as the EWGF: d/f and 4 inside one frame cell is a success, forward and neutral 1f each is the fastest. The game\'s maximum leniency is unconfirmed, so the mist-step EWGF limits apply. Right-stance JF Sky Rocket (more lenient) is not covered. The site judges the input condition only, not a real hit or frame advantage.',
