  // Bryan · Taunt Jet Upper (결정 37(tju)·34(char-select), 2026-10-15). Frame numbers come from the TJ constants
  'char.bryan.name':'Bryan', 'char.bryan.moves':'Taunt Jet Upper · Jet Upper · backdash',
  'move.tju':'Taunt Jet Upper', 'set.movesNote.bryan':'A move that is off is judged as if it did not exist. With Taunt Jet Upper off, the taunt (1+3+4) and the Jet Upper (f,n,b+2) are not judged and only the backdash is left. The Taunt Jet Upper tab always turns it on.',
  'set.tauntHelp':'1+3+4 key: one press is LP, LK and RK on the same frame (the taunt) — like assigning LP+LK+RK to one button in the game\'s controller settings. It only works for a character with a taunt.', 'touch.taunt':'Taunt',
  'mode.tju.name':'Taunt Jet Upper', 'tj.rankTitle':'Taunt Jet Upper ×10', 'log.tTj':'Taunt', 'log.tJu':'Jet Upper',
  'mode.tju.desc':()=>`Practice Bryan's taunt (1+3+4) into the Jet Upper (f,n,b+2). Counting the taunt press as 1f, the knee lands on ${TJ.KNEE_F}f, and only f on ${TJ_SIX}f · n on ${TJ_SIX+1}f · b+2 on ${TJ_GO}f makes the Jet Upper land on ${TJ_LAST}f (the end of the +${TJ.ADV}) for a combo. Check every frame on the timeline. The 10-try challenge goes to the leaderboard.`,
  'hint.tju':()=>`1+3+4 (taunt) → f on ${TJ_SIX}f · n on ${TJ_SIX+1}f · b+2 on ${TJ_GO}f · the 1+3+4 key is in the settings`,
  'mode.free.desc.bryan':'Free practice as Bryan. 1+3+4 = taunt, f,n,b+2 = Jet Upper, b,b = backdash. No wavedash and no Mishima moves.',
  'hint.free.bryan':()=>`1+3+4 = taunt · f,n,b+2 = Jet Upper · after the taunt f ${TJ_SIX}f · n ${TJ_SIX+1}f · b+2 ${TJ_GO}f = Taunt Jet Upper`,
  'pop.tju':'TAUNT JET UPPER!', 'pop.tjuStreak':n=>'TJU ×'+n+(n>=5?'!!':n===4?'!':''), 'pop.ju':'JET UPPER', 'pop.tauntDouble':'DOUBLE TAUNT', 'pop.guard':'GUARD',
  'tj.ju':'Jet Upper', 'tj.evaluation':'Taunt Jet Upper review', 'tj.ready':'Press the taunt (1+3+4) to see its frames', 'tj.timeline':'Taunt frame timeline',
  'tj.command':(f,b,go)=>'1+3+4 (taunt) · '+(go-2)+'f '+f+' · '+(go-1)+'f ★ · '+go+'f '+b+'+RP',
  'tj.guide':(knee,cancel,end,adv,last,ju,go)=>`The taunt press is 1f. The knee lands on ${knee}f (unblockable mid). The first input up to ${cancel}f cancels the taunt — on ${knee}f or earlier it cancels before the knee comes out. From ${cancel+1}f inputs are ignored and the taunt plays out to ${end}f. The knee gives +${adv}, so only a follow-up landing by ${last}f combos; the Jet Upper (${ju}f startup) needs b+2 on ${go}f with f and n on the two frames before it.`,
  'tj.legend':(knee,f6,n,go,last)=>`red ${knee}f = knee · gold ${f6}~${go}f = f · n · b+2 targets · green ${last}f = the last frame a follow-up can land and combo · bars below = the follow-up you pressed, its command and startup (green combo · red no combo)`,
