  // Fastest Jet Upper practice (결정 37(tju), 2026-10-16)
  'mode.ju.name':'Fastest Jet Upper',
  'mode.ju.desc':()=>`Practice Bryan's Jet Upper (f,n,b+2) on its own, without the taunt. The fastest input is f 1f · n 1f · b and RP on one frame: b+2 is the 3rd frame, so the ${TJ.JU_F}f Jet Upper lands ${TJ.JU_F+2}f after the f. The Taunt Jet Upper combos only with this fastest input (f on ${TJ_SIX}f · n on ${TJ_SIX+1}f · b+2 on ${TJ_GO}f). The timeline below counts the f as 1f and draws every frame of the input.`,
  'hint.ju':()=>`f,n,b+2 · fastest = f 1f · n 1f · b and RP on one frame (lands ${TJ.JU_F+2}f after the f)`,
  'ju.timeline':'Jet Upper frame timeline', 'ju.evaluation':'Fastest Jet Upper review', 'ju.ready':'Enter f,n,b+2 to see its frames',
  'ju.recent':'Recent inputs', 'ju.inCol':'Input', 'ju.help':'How the Fastest Jet Upper is judged',
  'ju.command':(f,n,b)=>'1f '+f+' · 2f '+n+' · 3f '+b+'+RP',
  'ju.guide':(su,fast,hit,six,go,axis)=>`The frame you press f is 1f. The fastest is f on 1f · neutral on 2f · b+2 on ${fast}f — with b+2 on frame ${fast} the ${su}f Jet Upper lands ${hit}f after the f. Press b and RP on the same frame: a b before the RP delays it by that much, an RP before the b brings out 2 (10f). In the Taunt Jet Upper this exact input has to go on ${six}~${go}f. The timeline runs to ${axis}f, the slowest input measured to still give a Jet Upper.`,
  'ju.legend':fast=>`gold 1~${fast}f = f · n · b+2 targets · top row = frames you held f · n · an early b (green 1f) · bottom row = frames from the f to the RP (green = the fastest ${fast}f)`,
  'ju.liveReady':(f,b,fast)=>'Counting starts on the frame you press '+f+' · the fastest has '+b+'+RP on '+fast+'f',
  'ju.liveRun':(f,fast)=>f+'f from the f · the fastest has b+2 on '+fast+'f', 'ju.liveDone':n=>'Last input '+n+'f · press f to count again',
  'ju.barIn':n=>'input '+n+'f',
  'ju.bar.ju':(su,total)=>'startup '+su+'f → lands '+total+'f after the f', 'ju.bar.slow':'outside the measured range — not checked', 'ju.bar.b2':'no neutral → b+2 (17f)', 'ju.bar.rp':'RP first → 2 (10f)',
  'ju.res.none':'No Jet Upper', 'ju.r.none':'No Jet Upper came out',
  'ju.sub.noSix':'no f before the RP', 'ju.sub.btns':b=>'RP with '+b, 'ju.sub.stale':n=>n+'f from the f to the RP — too slow', 'ju.sub.mixed':d=>d+' after the f', 'ju.sub.order':'not in f → n → b order',
  'ju.c.noSix':'No f was read before the RP. Hold f for at least one frame, then neutral → b+2 (a direction that comes and goes inside one frame is never read).',
  'ju.c.btns':b=>'RP and '+b+' came on the same frame, which reads as another move, not the Jet Upper. Press only b and RP.',
  'ju.c.stale':n=>`f → n → b was in order, but one direction was held over ${TJ_STALE_F}f, so it was not read as a Jet Upper (${n}f from the f to the RP). The measured range is f up to ${TJ.JU_F_MAX}f · n up to ${TJ.JU_N_MAX}f.`,
  'ju.c.mixed':d=>d+' came after the f, so the reading started over. Move straight f → neutral → b without passing a diagonal.',
  'ju.c.order':'It was not read in f → neutral → b+2 order. Check the order after the f on the timeline.',
  'ju.nNone':'none', 'ju.rpFirst':'RP first', 'ju.inLabel':'Input (f → RP)', 'ju.inTarget':(fast,hit)=>'fastest '+fast+'f · lands '+hit+'f after the f',
  'ju.fastCount':'Fastest', 'ju.rate':'Fastest rate', 'ju.juCount':'Jet Uppers out', 'ju.avg':(f,n,i)=>'Average of the inputs that gave a Jet Upper: f '+f+' · n '+n+' · input '+i,
  'ju.note':(su,fmax,nmax,bearly,axis,stale,six,go)=>`Uses the TEKKEN 8 Ver.3.02.02 practice-mode measurements as they are. The Jet Upper is f → n → b+2 (${su}f startup); on its own it was confirmed with f 1~${fmax}f · n 1~${nmax}f · b up to ${bearly}f before the RP (longer is "outside the measured range"; the ${axis}f timeline is that longest input). The fastest is f 1f · n 1f · b and RP on one frame, and the Taunt Jet Upper combos only when this input goes on ${six}~${go}f. With no neutral b+2 (17f) comes out, with the RP before the b 2 (10f). Inputs are read per 60Hz slot as its last direction and its buttons (one direction a frame, like the game). On a keyboard, the frame with f held and b added is neutral. A direction held over ${stale}f starts the reading over. On this tab every RP outside a taunt is a try (except an RP within ${su}f of the last try's RP, during its move). The site judges the input only and does not guarantee a real hit.`,
